{{!--
  The trick's difficulty value and where it comes from.

  Leads with the number, because that is what a reader wants first. The
  curator-published derivation formula follows: the operator-by-operator
  breakdown is pedagogy at trick level and always renders when published.
  The plain-words line restates the same components without the
  parenthesis-and-plus syntax, as a gloss for readers who don't parse
  formulas.

  Renders only when content.addAnalysis is non-null (= the trick has a
  curator-published resolved formula). Provenance is intentionally NOT
  rendered (curator-internal language).

  Per the 4-tier rendering hierarchy contract: Tier-4 patterns
  (xbody(N), dex(N), stall(N), spin(N), BOD(N), UNS(N)) appear ONLY on
  trick-detail pages + /freestyle/add-analysis; browse cards + landing
  forbid them via test-pinned absence.
--}}
{{#if content.addAnalysis}}
<section class="content-section trick-add-analysis" aria-label="Difficulty">
  <dl class="trick-add-analysis-fields">
    <dt>Difficulty</dt>
    <dd>
      <span class="trick-add-analysis-total">{{content.addAnalysis.totalAdd}} ADD</span>
      <code class="trick-add-analysis-derivation">{{content.addAnalysis.derivation}}</code>
      {{#if content.addAnalysis.derivationPlain}}
      <span class="trick-add-analysis-derivation-plain">{{content.addAnalysis.derivationPlain}}</span>
      {{/if}}
    </dd>
  </dl>
</section>
{{/if}}
